message: If you use this code, please cite the paper below.
type: article
title: "Beyond Band Importance: Signed Orientation-Aware Spectral Learning for Graph Fraud Detection"
authors:
  - given-names: Chunwei
    family-names: Tian
    affiliation: "School of Computer Science and Technology, Harbin Institute of Technology"
  - given-names: Qi
    family-names: Meng
    affiliation: "School of Computing and Data Science, The University of Hong Kong"
journal: "IEEE Transactions on Knowledge and Data Engineering"
year: 2026
publisher: "IEEE"
keywords:
  - graph fraud detection
  - graph neural networks
  - heterophily
  - spectral graph learning
license: MIT
abstract: >
  Spectral graph neural networks have shown strong potential for fraud
  detection by capturing graph signals across different frequency bands.
  Existing spectral approaches mainly assess which bands are informative,
  while paying less attention to which class each band favors. This paper
  proposes Signed Orientation-Aware Residual (SOAR), a spectral framework
  that preserves class-oriented evidence at the relation-band level.
